Decision #1 — File + constructor: NewSecurityEventWriter(*pgxpool.Pool) router.Writer
  - Mirrors the wrapper-pattern from NewSafetyWriter / NewLocationWriter / NewMediaWriter
  - Panics on nil pool (process-start fail-fast, same pattern as every prior 0011-0017 wrapper)
  - Compile-time assertion: var _ router.Writer = (*securityEventWriter)(nil)

Decision #2 — Bespoke (NOT composing snapshotWriter):
  - secEventDB local interface (Exec + QueryRow) — broader than snapshot_base.go's pgxPool because
    of the slow-path disambiguation requirement
  - Compile-time assertion: var _ secEventDB = (*pgxpool.Pool)(nil)
  - SQL is a single INSERT...SELECT...WHERE NOT EXISTS (per VIN RESOLUTION CONTRACT and Check 6
    reconciliation above)

Decision #3 — Idempotency via slow-path disambiguation:
  - Primary: securityEventInsertSQL — INSERT INTO security_events (vehicle_id, ts, event_type, to_state)
             SELECT v.id, $2, $3, $4 FROM vehicles v WHERE v.vin = $1
               AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM security_events se WHERE se.vehicle_id = v.id AND se.ts = $2 AND se.event_type = $3)
  - Slow path: securityEventVehicleExistsSQL — SELECT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM vehicles WHERE vin = $1)
  - Outcome matrix:
      RowsAffected == 1                           -> success (steady-state hot path, 1 round-trip)
      RowsAffected == 0 + vehicle exists          -> success (idempotent dup skip per Decision #3)
      RowsAffected == 0 + vehicle does NOT exist  -> error `vehicle not registered` (PII-clean, no VIN)
      Exec returns error                          -> error wrapped with prefix; slow-path NOT executed
      QueryRow.Scan returns error                 -> error wrapped with `disambiguation query` sub-prefix

Decision #4 — Field -> event_type mapping (3 entries today, snake_case canonical tokens per migration COMMENT):
  Locked            -> locked
  SentryMode        -> sentry_mode
  ValetModeEnabled  -> valet_mode_enabled
  from_state always NULL (not computable from a single atomic — downstream consumers reconstruct
    transitions from the per-(vehicle_id, event_type) ordered series)
  details always NULL (deferred to a future routing extension that wants to attach JSONB context)

Decision #5 — Tests:
  TestSecurityEventWriter_TypeMapMatchesRoutingYAML        — reflective coverage gate (count==3, no extras,
                                                              no missing, every entry e.Column == '')
  TestSecurityEventWriter_HappyPath_PerRoute               — 5 sub-cases: bool true/false for Locked,
                                                              bool true for ValetModeEnabled, Stringer for
                                                              SentryMode armed/off (covers both code paths
                                                              of bindSecurityEventState that production traffic hits)
  TestSecurityEventWriter_IdempotentDuplicate              — RowsAffected==0 + vehicle exists -> nil
  TestSecurityEventWriter_UnknownVehicle                   — RowsAffected==0 + vehicle absent -> error,
                                                              VIN-omission PII rule pinned
  TestSecurityEventWriter_UnknownFieldReturnsError         — VehicleSpeed (routed elsewhere) -> error,
                                                              widening guard pinned
  TestSecurityEventWriter_BindStateRejectsBadValues        — 6 sub-cases: nil, int, float64, []byte,
                                                              empty string, empty Stringer
  TestSecurityEventWriter_DBExecErrorWrapped               — sentinel unwrap + prefix; slow-path NOT
                                                              issued when primary errors
  TestSecurityEventWriter_DBQueryErrorWrapped              — slow-path failure mode + `disambiguation query`
                                                              sub-prefix + sentinel unwrap
  TestSecurityEventWriter_TimestampNormalisation           — non-UTC monotonic ts -> equivalent UTC bound
  TestNewSecurityEventWriter_NilPoolPanics                 — constructor fail-fast
  TestSecurityEventWriter_SatisfiesRouterWriter            — runtime mirror of the compile-time assertion

  In-file test fakes: secEventRecorder (Exec+QueryRow), secEventRow (Scan), stubStringer (fmt.Stringer
  stand-in for proto enums). Recorder is local to security_event_writer_test.go because the shared
  recorder in snapshot_base_test.go does not implement QueryRow and that file is not in the
  allowed-files list.

